      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Major Cost Drivers in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Complexity & Pitch: A steep pitch (hazardous to walk on) or a roof with multi-level walkout basements adds roughly $25 to $150+ to the baseline bill due to the safety equipment required ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Home Size: Most standard pricing is structured around a 1,500 to 2,000 sq ft home footprint. Larger homes or commercial structures can see higher rates, sometimes translating to square-footage pricing ($0.05 to $0.10 per sq ft) for major commercial real estate."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Certifications vs. Visual Checks: If you are buying a home or renewing insurance and need a formal, signed roof certification report, expect a company to add an extra $75 to $200 to the cost of the evaluation ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Are \"Free\" Inspections Actually Free?"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you suspect recent storm damage or believe you need a total replacement, many localized contractors\u2014like Intermountain West Contractors or Vertex Roofing\u2014will offer a free visual inspection as part of a consultation package. Be aware that these free checks are intended to scope out structural damage for future repair bids or insurance claims rather than provide formal paperwork for a real estate closing ."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down options, are you looking for this inspection to buy/sell a home, resolve a hidden leak, or assess storm damage? Let me know your general city or county in Utah, and I can suggest a few well-reviewed local outfits!"
      },
